#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# nonpositive_rationals

#% text
# `nonpositive_rationals` is the domain of the rational numbers that are less than or equal to 0.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `element(x, nonpositive_rationals)` decides numbers and gives `element(x, rationals) and x <= 0` for a symbol.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
element(-2/3, nonpositive_rationals)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(1/2, nonpositive_rationals)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
element(x, nonpositive_rationals)
#% output
#= element(x, rationals) and x <= 0

#% cell
reduce((2*x^2 - 1)*(4*x^2 - 1) == 0, x, nonpositive_rationals)
#% output
#= x == -1/2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `nonnegative_rationals`, `negative_rationals`, `rationals`
